The Proof of Concept (PoC) shall include:
1. documented technical collaboration with the antenna component supplier;
2. a complete simulation report as defined in Chapter [X];
3. a demonstration that the prototype hardware meets all specified performance values; and
4. measurement results obtained at the vehicle level.

Upon reaching the start-end engine speed threshold, the system shall initiate the drive-off sequence if at least one of the following conditions is met:
1. The upper clutch switch is active;
2. The clutch pedal position sensor value is greater than the clutch pedal active threshold (50% calibration) AND the clutch pedal position sensor value is plausible;
3. The gas pedal value is greater than the minimum gas pedal threshold (5% calibration).

The system shall output a unique error code for each of the following blockage conditions:
a) blockage detected during self-test or power-on;
b) far-range blockage detected during normal operation;
c) near-range sensor blockage.

The Front Panel shall include the following components:
1. one black panel manufactured using foil technology and composed of plastic;
2. one galvanized and laser-etched eject switch;
3. one disc slot; and
4. [X] light guides.

The CPS shall detect and report the occurrence of any of the following failure modes within [X] ms:
1. Open circuit (interruption) on the sensor supply, sensor output, or sensor ground lines;
2. Short circuit on the sensor supply, sensor output, or sensor ground lines;
3. Any internal failure mode defined in [Reference Document/Section].

Detection shall be performed accounting for the shunt resistances specified in Chapter 8.3.2.

The High Voltage Interlock Loop (HVIL) shall transition to an "interrupted" state if any of the following conditions occur:
1. The HVIL signal loop is opened;
2. The HVIL signal is lost;
3. The HVIL signal is short-circuited to Low Voltage (LV+) supply; or
4. The HVIL signal is short-circuited to vehicle ground.

Each sensor shall perform self-diagnostic checks to detect the following fault conditions:
1. Electrical circuit faults: short to battery, short to ground, and open circuit;
2. Signal out-of-range faults: signal values outside the defined physical operating range;
3. Signal plausibility faults: signal stuck (no change in value over time) and signal bias (constant offset from expected value).

The system shall perform a lifetime assurance test on two (2) cells using Test Number az1 and Cyclic Art, subject to the following parameters:
1. Deloading Current: 15.5C;
2. Mean Energy Level: 31 Wh (representing 55% State of Charge at End of Life);
3. Energy Deloaded per Cycle: 50.8 Wh (representing 90% State of Charge at End of Life);
4. Current Pulse Duration: 20 seconds;
5. Current Break Duration: The minimum time required to allow for temperature regeneration;
6. Daily Operational Time: 4.5 hours.

5. The player application shall provide the following playback control functions to each concurrent user:
5.1. Standard controls: playlist browsing, play, pause, skip track, and seek within track;
5.2. Auto-playback: automatic initiation of playback when a new media source becomes available;
5.3. Auto-pause: automatic suspension of playback upon receipt of an incoming phone call;
5.4. Playtime last mode: automatic resumption of audiobooks from the last recorded playback position;
5.5. Play similar: initiation of playback of tracks categorized by the same genre or musical style as the current track.
